<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xiang Yan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 223 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xiang Yan was a general of the State of Chu in the last years of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a>. In 225 BCE he defeated a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-xin-qin">Li Xin</a>, but in 224 BCE Qin sent a much larger force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-jian-qin">Wang Jian</a>, which crushed his army. He died in 223 BCE as Qin completed its conquest of Chu. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> later led the rebellion against the Qin dynasty.</p></div>
